00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.600
So let's start today with some policy analysis.&nbsp;
Nothing, nothing more exciting than that for sure.&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.120
But this is actually very interesting. We've&nbsp;
talked before. In fact, we spoke earlier on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.880
the bonus show yesterday about this. But I do&nbsp;
want to do a deeper dove on it because it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:22.720
very important. A conservative think tank did an&nbsp;
analysis of Joe Biden's tax plan and confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:30.160
that the tax increases will go almost exclusively&nbsp;
to the very rich and will be stimulative to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:37.200
economy overall. And this is so wild because it's&nbsp;
so obvious when you look at Joe Biden's tax plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:44.080
that the tax hikes go overwhelmingly to the&nbsp;
top five and one percent. And yet Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.600
and Trump not only have been lying about what's&nbsp;
in the plan, they lie about the impact that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.880
plan will have. So let's set it up and go through&nbsp;
it piece by piece. When Donald Trump was running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:02.800
for president back in 2015, 2016 and proposed his&nbsp;
tax plan, nonpartisan groups looked at it and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.600
said this is not going to stimulate the economy&nbsp;
and it will blow up the deficit. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.960
every time Donald Trump was asked about it, when&nbsp;
Trump's advisers were asked about it, they would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:19.680
say, I don't know what they're not calculating.&nbsp;
Is that the tax plan will grow the economy so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.840
that we will get new tax revenue. So even though&nbsp;
it might in the short term look like it increases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:32.080
the deficit, the growth aspect will weigh&nbsp;
override that and we're going to get more tax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.320
revenue and the economy will grow in all this&nbsp;
different stuff. The deficit will actually go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.960
down. We knew it wouldn't happen at the time and&nbsp;
it hasn't happened. Donald Trump gave tax cuts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.240
the rich. The deficit exploded. The growth hasn't&nbsp;
happened. And this is before. Corona virus. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.120
Corona virus has thrown a monkey wrench into&nbsp;
the entire thing. But even pre coronavirus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.920
it wasn't happening. So Joe Biden puts out a&nbsp;
tax plan and the tax plan includes a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:02.160
different provisions, higher taxes for the very&nbsp;
rich. He would uncap Social Security taxes beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:08.240
four hundred thousand dollars in annual income,&nbsp;
huge revenue increase. He would tax capital gains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.880
as ordinary income in certain cases for certain&nbsp;
people earning over a million dollars a year. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:18.160
would eliminate the stepped up basis loophole. I&nbsp;
don't have to explain each item. But the point is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:24.080
Joe Biden puts out a specific tax plan. We look at&nbsp;
it and it's unremarkable, given our understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:30.400
of economics, that Joe Biden's tax plan would work&nbsp;
perfectly reasonably if indeed it is made law.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.440
Donald Trump has been hammering on Biden's tax&nbsp;
plan by saying things like he will quadruple your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.400
taxes, mathematical impossibility if you already&nbsp;
pay 35 percent. How do you quadruple? That doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:46.400
make any sense. Trump says under Biden's tax plan,&nbsp;
your Forell one case would implode. We would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.880
a recession. We would have a depression. All of&nbsp;
that different stuff. And Donald Trump has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.920
saying Biden will raise your taxes if you are&nbsp;
in the middle class. If you're a middle class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.280
American, Joe Biden will raise your taxes. Biden,&nbsp;
he clearly has said he wouldn't do it. OK, now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:07.760
financial firms like Goldman Sachs have already&nbsp;
looked at the plan and they've confirmed what any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:14.160
reasonable person would realize when looking at&nbsp;
the plan and understanding history, which is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:20.080
Joe Biden's tax plan would likely grow the&nbsp;
economy. We know the economy tends to do better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.600
under Democratic presidents. We can debate why. We&nbsp;
can debate whether it does better enough. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.720
reality is any indicator you look at inflation,&nbsp;
stock market, job creation, unemployment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:37.280
GDP growth. Historically, they do better under&nbsp;
Democratic presidents. OK, but now incomes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:41.920
the right wing think tank, the American Enterprise&nbsp;
Institute. This is, again, a right wing think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:48.800
tank. They've analyzed the plan and they agree&nbsp;
that no one, almost all of the tax increases that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:56.240
Joe Biden proposes go to the richest five percent&nbsp;
of households. And that Joe Biden's tax plan will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:04.640
reduce taxes for the bottom 95 percent of Howth&nbsp;
households. So top five percent, your taxes go up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:12.160
Bottom 95 percent taxes go down. Biden's tax&nbsp;
plan, according to the right wing think tank AEI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.400
will raise federal revenue by nearly three&nbsp;
trillion dollars over the next decade. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:24.720
would be deficit negative. And then here is&nbsp;
the real kicker. All of this stuff Biden is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:31.920
going to do. Trump says it will destroy the&nbsp;
economy. Okay. All of it over 10 years will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:40.240
lower GDP. Get ready for this by zero point one&nbsp;
six percent. OK. That's essentially nothing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:46.720
Zero point one six percent decrease the GDP over&nbsp;
a decade. But and here's the really amazing thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:53.840
Demand side stimulus works, my friends. Biden's&nbsp;
plan is going to take some of that tax money and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:58.720
spend it on social investments, which will&nbsp;
increase economic growth. So in other words.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:09.440
The direct impact of Biden's tax plan is an almost&nbsp;
zero decrease of GDP of point one six percent over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:15.360
10 years. But it will create growth. This is what&nbsp;
Trump claimed his plan would do, even though it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:23.760
wouldn't. Biden's plan would create growth such&nbsp;
that new tax revenues would exceed the cost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.640
And we are expecting that GDP would actually&nbsp;
increase more quickly thanks to this plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.440
This is exactly what Donald Trump claimed his&nbsp;
plan would do. It didn't. It was never going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:39.760
to. But even a right wing think tank acknowledges&nbsp;
that it is exactly what Joe Biden's plan would do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:45.840
We are in bizarro world with Republican voters&nbsp;
continuing to fall for Trump's claims that Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:51.840
will be bad for the economy. That Biden will tax&nbsp;
the middle class more. He won't. And by the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:57.680
even if you want to argue that this will be bad&nbsp;
